\description{
Simulates a \code{malariasimulation} parameter list one day at a time, resolving
each day in the order \code{malariasimulation} does: immunity decay, biting and
infection, one competing draw per person between infection and progression,
a day of the mosquito model, and deaths replaced by births. The first three
arguments match \code{malariasimulation::run_simulation()}. \code{vignette("model")}
specifies the model.
}
\details{
The seed is where \code{malariasimulation} seeds: the
\code{malariaEquilibrium} solution for \code{init_EIR} (\code{malariaEquilibriumVivax} for
\emph{P. vivax}), with the humans under the treatment coverage in force at
timestep 0 and the mosquitoes sized under the coverage at timestep 1, as
\code{set_equilibrium()} and the IBM's initialisation do. It is close to the
daily model's fixed point but not on it, so outputs relax over the first
years. A seasonal run is seeded at the annual-mean (aseasonal) equilibrium
and oscillates around a limit cycle rather than holding flat. Use a
burned-in window for calibration and comparison; \code{vignette("using")} gives
the relaxation and settling times.

A run in which any compartment falls below zero stops with an error naming
the day and the age group. Each day an age group loses its ageing and
mortality fraction out of the same stock as its infections, and several
consecutive groups a day or two wide can lose more than they hold at an EIR
in the hundreds; widen them in \code{age_lower} (\code{\link[=ode_tuning]{ode_tuning()}}).
}
